guamp: FN/FT rows count draws by fragment function, full-screen surface layers and passes into surfaces without RenderTarget (0064)

Measures for the HakiOS ideas (analisi/hakios-confronto-20261107.md, ideas 1, 2, 5; ideas only, no code taken). Two report rows after
PU, deltas since the last report:
  FN rt<passes into a surface texture made without RenderTarget (rendered through a stand-in)> fs<draws whose fragment texture 0 is a
     surface of 0.9 Mpx or more>/<of them static: surface seed unchanged since its previous such draw>/<their kpx>k
     lb<luma_boost draws>/<passes>/<pass kpx>k ed<edr_scale likewise>
  FT the three fragment functions ("_frag", "_lph", "_lpf" dropped) whose passes covered the most render-area kpx: name:passes/kpx k/draws
The fragment function's slot is found once at pipeline creation (24 slots); a draw adds two atomics, and the pass area once per function
per pass. backboardd's pipelines.log (crash-ios 20261104-160143, 114 boots) shows luma_boost_lph made once every boot since boot 13 and
no edr_scale at all; the rows tell whether luma_boost runs every frame and how many kpx the blur chain (downsample/narrow_blur/
variable_blur, the backdrop behind dock and widgets) and static full-screen layers (wallpaper) cost before a cache or a substitute is
written. NMB_FN_ROW=0 (guamp-m2v-env) turns the counting off. Two rows more: the rows past the 48th of the dump are dropped.
Applies after 0051 (the PU row); the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI (new code checked with clang -fsyntax-only on stubs).

